  "observations": "The original live technique swung the upper legs independently and folded the forelegs under an upright body. Attack, cast and recoil now solve upper leg, knee and paw together. The complete source and rebuilt battle assets were visually inspected across all 13 clips. All 16 production transition sequences were inspected at low and medium quality. All nine inspector technique choices were inspected front and side; Open Wound was also inspected from the opposite side and three-quarter view. No disconnected legs, folded-under forelegs, muzzle/cheek collapse or floor-clipping support paws were seen. The first full-source candidate inspection covered another 36 sheets and 216 frames before this separate final battle-model pass. This certifies Oni only; the renewed independent full-roster audit remains unfinished.",
